# Canonical starting puzzle: every executable byte is a literal binary token.
11111010 # instruction | CLI | Keep the final halt stopped.
10111011 00000000 00000000 # instruction | MOV BX,0 | Initialize the success marker.
10111000 11111111 11111111 # instruction | MOV AX,FFFF | Start at the unsigned upper boundary.
00000101 00000001 00000000 # instruction | ADD AX,1 | The result wraps to zero, setting both CF and ZF.
01110011 00000011 # instruction | JAE +3 | JAE tests CF=0, so this branch fails despite ZF=1.
10111011 00000001 00000000 # instruction | MOV BX,1 | Mark the unwanted fall-through path.
11110100 # instruction | HLT | Stop with BX=1.
